# The game profile: where the tools find the game, the BIOS, the test harness and the lifter's
# ABI export, and the game's own constants. Change a path here, not in the tools.
#
# One KEY=VALUE per line; comments on lines of their own; no spaces or quotes in values.
# ${ROOT} is the root of the checkout the tool runs in. A workflow worktree links roms/, bn6f/
# and build-tools/ to the main checkout's (SHARED in tools/wf/wf/tools/build.py).
# Read by shell scripts through tools/common.sh, by Python through tools/gamepaths.py (tools/wf too),
# and by tools/Makefile.

# The disassembly (submodule). It assembles the original game, byte-identical to the SHA-1 in bn6f.sha1.
BN6F_DIR=${ROOT}/bn6f
ORIG_ROM=${ROOT}/bn6f/bn6f.gba
ORIG_ELF=${ROOT}/bn6f/bn6f.elf
ORIG_SHA1=${ROOT}/bn6f/bn6f.sha1

# Your own dump of the GBA BIOS (16 KB, SHA-1 300c20df6731a33952ded8c436f7f186d25d3492).
# Git ignores roms/: never commit it. Every check boots both games through it; ./build.sh does not need it.
GBA_BIOS=${ROOT}/roms/gba_bios.bin

# The test harness (headless mGBA) and the trace recorder, built by `make -C tools` (git-ignored).
MGBA_RUN=${ROOT}/build-tools/mgba_run
RECORD=${ROOT}/build-tools/record

# The game's frame counter: the toolkit's CurFramePtr field (toolkit 0x020093B0 + oToolkit_CurFramePtr 0x24)
# points to the u16 that counts game frames. Recorded routes are keyed to it (mgba_run --game-frame-addr),
# so a replay gives the game the same input whatever the speed of the build.
GAME_FRAME_ADDR=0x020093D4

# Recorded gameplay routes (NAME.trace, with NAME.sav and NAME.poke when they exist).
TRACES=${ROOT}/tools/traces

# Checkpoints of long routes (tools/import_route.py): NAME/NAME_GGGGGGG.state, the original game's
# state at the start of game frame G, and NAME_GGGGGGG.prof, the profile of the window from it.
# Game RAM: git ignores build-*/, never commit them. Worktrees link it to the main checkout's.
CHECKPOINTS=${ROOT}/build-checkpoints

# The lifter's calling-convention export (lift.py --export-abi ABI_GRAPH) and what tools/abi derives
# from it (captures.json, summary.json). Kept out of build/, the old PC port's CMake folder.
ABI_DIR=${ROOT}/build-abi
ABI_GRAPH=${ROOT}/build-abi/graph.json
